_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 4
---
order: 4
---
short_label: IX.4
---
statement: If a cubic number multiplied by a cubic number makes some number, then the product is a cube.
---
proof:

Let the cubic number *A* multiplied by the cubic number *B* make *C.*

I say that *C* is cubic.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="270" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IX.4 diagram" src="propIX4.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IX.4",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "B0;point;free;-1000,75;0;0",
            "B3;point;free;1000,75;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;-1000,110;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;1000,110;0;0",
            "D0;point;free;-1000,145;0;0",
            "D3;point;free;1000,145;0;0",
            "U1;point;free;1000,0;0;0",
            "U2;point;free;1000,35;0;0",
            "A1;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0;0",
            "A2;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,100,0;0",
            "A;line;connect;A1,A2;black",
            "B1;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,30,0;0",
            "B2;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,135,0;0",
            "B;line;connect;B1,B2;black",
            "C1;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,30,0;0",
            "C2;point;proportion;U1,U2,A1,A2,B1,B2,C1,C3;0",
            "C;line;connect;C1,C2;black",
            "D1;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,30,0;0",
            "D2;point;proportion;U1,U2,A1,A2,A1,A2,D1,D3;0",
            "D;line;connect;D1,D2;black"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Multiply *A* by itself to make *D.* Then *D* is a cube. [!just IX.3]

Since *A* multiplied by itself makes *D,* and multiplied by *B* makes *C,* therefore *A* is to *B* as *D* is to *C.* And, since *A* and *B* are cubic numbers, therefore *A* and *B* are similar solid numbers. Therefore two mean proportional numbers fall between *A* and *B,* so that two mean proportional numbers fall between *D* and *C* also. [!just VII.17; VIII.19; VIII.8]

And *D* is a cube, therefore *C* is also a cube. [!just VIII.23]

Therefore, *if a cubic number multiplied by a cubic number makes some number, then the product is cubic.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
---
body:

Of course, *m*<sup>3</sup>*n*<sup>3</sup> = (*mn*)<sup>3</sup>.
